# Email and SMS notifications

In-app bells stay immediate. **Email and SMS** follow this policy. Canonical code: `server/src/notifyQuietHours.ts`, `server/src/messageDigestNotify.ts`, `server/src/listingFirstSeekerNotify.ts`.

## Quiet hours (listing-local)

- Do **not** send notification email or SMS from **23:00** through **06:00** local. Resume at **06:01**.
- Timezone = city of the listing(s) in that notify (`resolveTimeZoneForListingCity`); if none, `America/Mexico_City`.
- At most **one** send is stored overnight. 3-hour reminder slots do **not** stack (no 2am + 5am emails). The due send goes at 06:01; `last_message_digest_at` then restarts the 3-hour clock.
- **Never** apply quiet hours to OTP, password-reset, claim, or ARCO confirmation SMS/email.

## 3-hour digest

Unread-message emails: at most one every **3 hours** while unread (`MESSAGE_DIGEST_DEBOUNCE_MS`). First new-seeker listing message in a window: send email (+ SMS if below) immediately unless quiet hours or already inside a 3-hour wait.

## First-seeker SMS (temporary)

Kill switch: `LISTING_FIRST_SEEKER_SMS=0`. Default on when SMS Masivos is configured.

- Only the **first listing chat** from that seeker to this **publisher** (any of their posts). Same seeker, later rooms or follow-ups: no extra SMS.
- Immediate with that first in-app bell **unless** another new seeker already started a 3-hour wait — then one aggregated SMS with the next digest.
- Copy: `server/src/listingFirstSeekerSms.ts`. **SMS Masivos cap = 160 characters** (the API rejects longer listing SMS). First name only. Single seeker: `te escribió por tu post "{4–6 word title lead}"` (use as many letters as the budget allows, `…` if clipped). Footer: `Revisa tu correo regularmente (también spam) o entra en bestie.mx/mensajes`. Two people: `{first} y otro usuario`. Three+: `{first} y otros N usuarios`.
- Requires verified +52 phone and `phone_notify_opt_in`. Do not SMS chat body.
